# EC2 AMI AutoScaling Updater

This AWS Lambda function automates the process of updating an Auto Scaling Group (ASG) with the latest AMI created from a specific EC2 instance. It:

- Retrieves the most recent AMI using EC2 `describe_images`.
- Creates a new version of an existing Launch Template with the updated AMI.
- Updates the specified ASG to use the new launch template version.
- Triggers an instance refresh using a rolling deployment strategy.

## Use Case

Perfect for automated patching or deploying updated configurations via AMIs, ensuring your ASG always runs the latest instance version.

## Technologies

- Python 3.x
- AWS Lambda
- Boto3 (AWS SDK for Python)
- Auto Scaling
- EC2 AMIs
--------------
Once the function is created test it and if it works then go to Cloudwatch and createa a log group that call the lambda function has often as you need.
